\p \v 9 \w What|strong="H4100"\w* \w does the worker|strong="H6213"\w* \w gain|strong="H3504"\w* \w from his|strong="H1931"\w* \w toil|strong="H6001"\w*? \v 10 \w I have seen|strong="H7200"\w* \w the burden|strong="H6045"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w God|strong="H430"\w* \w has laid|strong="H5414"\w* \w upon the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of men|strong="H120"\w* \w to occupy|strong="H6031"\w* them. \v 11 \w He has made|strong="H6213"\w* \w everything|strong="H3605"\w* \w beautiful|strong="H3303"\w* \w in its time|strong="H6256"\w*. \w He has also|strong="H1571"\w* \w set|strong="H5414"\w* \w eternity|strong="H5769"\w* \w in the hearts of men|strong="H3820"\w*, \w yet|strong="H1097"\w* \w they|strong="H120"\w* \w cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w fathom|strong="H4672"\w* \w the work|strong="H4639"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w God|strong="H430"\w* \w has done|strong="H6213"\w* \w from beginning|strong="H7218"\w* \w to|strong="H5704"\w* \w end|strong="H5490"\w*.
